To run a new liquid, 

four files are needed as in the MCliquid test job -
liqzmat
dummy.z
liqpar
liqcmd

For example, to run pure liquid methanol with OPLS-AA,
I copied these files from boss/testjobs/MCliquid to a new directory.
Then, I modified them slightly as follows.

liqzmat:
To obtain the input methanol Z-matrix,
(1) I copied ~/boss/aazmat/meoh.z to this directory 
(2) executed the script xSPM (xSPM meoh). All scripts are in boss/scripts
    This script expands the Z-matrix to the style needed for solvents.
(3) made 1 minor edit to the output file "sum" -
    Changed the title line (first line) to only have a 5-character name.
(4) renamed sum liqzmat

dummy.z:
(5) In dummy.z, I changed ethanol to methanol. This is cosmetic.

liqpar:
(6) In liqpar, I changed the center atom for the solvent
    molecules from 5 to 1 (the oxygen). Atom 5 (carbon) would have been OK.
    I checked the atoms for the solvent-solvent rdfs and made no changes.

liqcmd:
(7) no changes needed

To execute:
I edited liqcmd to make a liqcmdshort that runs just 100 configurations
instead of 500000 for each MC run. 
Then execute:
csh liqcmdshort >& log &
The output all looked OK, so I submitted the full job:
csh liqcmd >& log &

This ran 2M configurations of equilibration followed by 2M configurations of averaging.
The last output file is liqote2. I note in this file
 NMOL = 267          EDGE =   26.2363   26.2363   26.2363    RCUT =   11.0000
 NACCPT = 2000000    NRJECT = 1122065    MXCON = 500000      NCON =  500000
So, the acceptance rate of (2000000-1122065)/2000000 = 44% is reasonable.
I also note at the end of the output:
