The energy is pretty stable, but the volume is decreasing still.
I would restart the averaging and run at least another 5M configurations
to obtain more precise averages. It is so fast now that even more could be run.
To run the 5M averaging:
csh liqavcmd >& log &

The density from the last run is: N*MW/0.6023*V = 267*32.04/.6023*18077 = 0.786 g/cc. 
The value in JACS 118, 11225 is 0.779 for OPLS-AA and 0.786 for experiment at 
25 C and 1 atm.

To compute the heat of vaporization, one should do a gas-phase MC calculation
(see the MCgas test job); however,

dHvap = E(gas) - E(liq) + RT = E(gas) - Einter(liq) -Eintra(liq) + RT
      = ca. -Einter(liq) + RT
      = -(-350.461 -1922.524)/267 + 0.6 = 9.11 kcal/mol
The value in JACS 118, 11225 is 8.95 and the exptl value is 8.95.

Note also that the average intramolecular energy is 1922.524/267 = 7.20 kcal/mol.
The value in JACS 118, 11225 is 7.23 and the gas-phase value is 7.08. The monomer
distort some in the liquid to enhance the hydrogen bonding, and note
dHvap = 7.08 - (-350.461)/267 + RT = 8.99 kcal/mol

